  "query_preview": "..\n\nA parade of upper lows will move through the western United \nStates this coming week. Monday will be in-between systems with\ntransient ridging providing a modest warm up and near normal\nhighs. The next upper low with an associated front will move \nthrough on Tuesday, though the focus of this low will be mainly \nto the north through central-northern Arizona. This front will \nbring shower chances from western Pima in the morning towards \nthe New Mexico border in the evening, with lower chances on the \nsouthern end. Overall rain amounts should be fairly light with \nthe forecast ranging from a few hundredths to around two tenths \nof an inch, with Pinal and northern Graham-Greenlee seeing the \nupper end of the spectrum. Temperatures will cool a few degrees \nand surface winds will turn out of the southwest and increase to\n12-18 mph with afternoon gusts to 30 mph.\n\nAnother trough passage will likely occur Friday into Saturday,\nthough current ensembles favor keeping precipitation well to the\nnorth again. Temperatures bounce up to near normal ahead of this\ntrough on Thursday then fall below normal Friday into the\nweekend.",
